# ─── AI providers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitTidy tries Gemini first, then falls back to OpenRouter. Configure at least
# one. Both are free tiers. See docs/GEMINI-SETUP.md for a phone walkthrough.

# Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (no credit card).
# Recommended — schema-enforced JSON removes the "model replied with prose"
# failure entirely, and the free quota is far larger than OpenRouter's.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides. Model names change; check ai.google.dev if generation
# always falls through to OpenRouter.
GEMINI_MODEL=
GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS=

# Fallback provider. Server-only — never prefix with VITE_.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=baidu/cobuddy:free
# Comma-separated. Use ONLY :free models so this never costs money.
OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_MODELS=

# ─── GitHub OAuth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# `repo` covers private repositories. Set `public_repo` to drop private access
# entirely — the safer choice if you only tidy public repos.
GITHUB_OAUTH_SCOPE=repo

# Optional. Sent to OpenRouter as HTTP-Referer.
PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://git-tidy.vercel.app
